The TypeScript adaptation accepts only plain decimal option values, refuses
expressions, exponents, signs, hexadecimal, inf/nan, trailing text, escaping
and float32 rounding midpoints instead of approximating them, always writes a
new owned output frame, declares the per-channel ring in reserve(), enforces
explicit allocation limits and AbortSignal, and adds no FFmpeg runtime code.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
